# Allowlist, not blocklist.
#
# A blocklist has to predict what junk appears in the deploy directory, and it
# always loses: on prod the context had grown to 1.28 GB (31 s just to transfer)
# from files nobody thought to exclude. Denying everything and naming what the
# build actually reads cannot regress that way.
#
# Verified with `go list -deps ./cmd/api ./cmd/worker`: the import graph touches
# only cmd, internal and openapi. migrations and scripts are copied into the
# final image by the Dockerfile.
*

!go.mod
!go.sum
!cmd
!internal
!openapi
!migrations
!scripts

# Test fixtures are never compiled into the binaries.
internal/service/testdata
